.TH CHANGELOG-ADD 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog add \- create a new changelog fragment file describing a single change
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog add
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBadd\fR command creates a new YAML fragment file in the fragments directory.
Each fragment describes one discrete change (bugfix, enhancement, deprecation, etc.)
with metadata including issue reference, category, date, and human-readable title.

Fragments are the primary unit of changelog content. They accumulate over time as
developers add entries describing their work, then get aggregated into release notes
by \fBchangelog release\fR or \fBchangelog generate\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
.B Required:
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-issue\fR=\fIID\fR
Issue or JIRA ID associated with this change (e.g., "PG\-001", "BUG\-12345").
.PP
This becomes the fragment filename and is used for deduplication. Must be unique
within the fragments directory.

.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-text\fR=\fITEXT\fR
Body text content of the fragment in markdown format.
.PP
Supports multi-line content with proper YAML quoting. Use double quotes for strings
containing colons to avoid PyYAML parsing issues.

.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-category\fR=\fICATEGORY\fR
Category of change being documented. Determines which section the fragment appears in.
.PP
Valid categories:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIbugfixes\fR (default) \- Bug fixes and corrections
.IP \(bu 2
\fImajor_changes\fR \- Major new features or breaking changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fiminor_changes\fR \- Minor improvements and enhancements
.IP \(bu 2
\fIbreaking_changes\fR \- Breaking changes requiring migration guides
.IP \(bu 2
\fIdeprecated_features\fR \- Features marked for removal in future releases
.IP \(bu 2
\fIremoved_features\fR \- Previously deprecated features now removed
.IP \(bu 2
\fIsecurity_fixes\fR \- Security vulnerability fixes
.IP \(bu 2
\fIknown_issues\fR \- Documented known issues or workarounds
.RE

.TP
.B Optional:
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-title\fR=\fITITLE\fR
Human-readable title for the fragment. Appears in changelog output above the body text.
If omitted, defaults to "Fragment #\fI<issue>\fR".

.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Output directory for the fragment file. Defaults to \fIchangelogs/fragments/\fR in the current project root.
.PP
Useful for adding fragments to alternative fragment directories or notes directories.

.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Read fragment body text from an existing file instead of using \fB\-\-text\fR.
.PP
Useful when the fragment content is long or already written to a temporary file.

.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR=\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR
Date for this change in YYYY-MM-DD format. Defaults to today's date if not specified.
.PP
Used for sorting and chronological ordering of fragments within releases.
.SH FRAGMENT FORMAT
.PP
Fragments are stored as YAML files with the following structure:
.IP \(bu 2
Filename: \fI<issue>-<category>.yml\fR (e.g., "PG-001-bugfixes.yml")
.IP \(bu 2
Content: YAML with category key mapping to an array of change entries

Example fragment file (\fIPG\-001\-bugfixes.yml\fR):
.nf
    bugfixes:
      - text: |
          Fixed crash when processing large files.
        title: "Stability improvement"
.fi
.PP
The tool automatically handles proper YAML quoting and formatting to ensure fragments
parse correctly regardless of special characters in the content.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Add a simple bugfix fragment (uses defaults):
.nf
    changelog add \\
        --issue PG-001 \\
        --text "Fixed crash when processing large files"
.fi

.TP
Add an enhancement with custom title and date:
.nf
    changelog add \\
        --category minor_changes \\
        --issue IMP-456 \\
        --title "Added support for parallel processing" \\
        --text "Implemented multi-threaded file processing that improves performance by 10x." \\
        --date 2026-07-15
.fi

.TP
Add a breaking change with detailed description:
.nf
    changelog add \\
        --category breaking_changes \\
        --issue API-789 \\
        --title "Removed deprecated --legacy flag" \\
        --text "The --legacy flag was removed in v1.0. Use the new --modern equivalent instead."
.fi

.TP
Add fragment from an existing file:
.nf
    changelog add \\
        --issue DOC-123 \\
        --file /tmp/fragment-body.md \\
        --title "Documentation updates"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-lint(8)\fR \- Validate fragment files for correctness
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate release notes from accumulated fragments
.TP
\fBchangelog-config(5)\fR \- Configuration file reference
